We have a large group of people from around the world

85
00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.160
who are doing great things and creating and building

86
00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.800
a lot of great things with AI

87
00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:59.920
that I think being able to form that connection

88
00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:01.760
will definitely open doors for you

89
00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.240
as you build out your practice

90
00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:06.200
selling AI and AI agents as a service for people.

91
00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.280
But now, before we dive into the content,

92
00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:10.440
I think there's three principles that I want to impart

93
00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:13.000
to set you up for success over the next eight weeks.

94
00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.480
The first principle is what's called the transition curve.

95
00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.320
And the transition curve sometimes called

96
00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:19.120
the emotional cycle of change

97
00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:21.160
was basically developed by psychologists

98
00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:23.720
sometime in the 1970s, and it still holds up today.

99
00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:27.040
Essentially, what it does is it maps your own emotional journey

100
00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.240
for any significant change that you will undertake.

101
00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:32.000
And that includes the transformation that you are undergoing

102
00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.960
now where you will go from an AI hobbyist

103
00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:35.600
to an AI service provider.

104
00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.360
And there's four stages here.

105
00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.000
The first one, which you likely are in right now

106
00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.640
is uninformed optimism, which is a great place to be

107
00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:43.800
because you have that optimism.

108
00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.040
You're very excited and everything seems possible

109
00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:47.160
and you can't wait to start.

110
00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.240
And it's obviously something that you need to enjoy.

111
00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:50.680
But what's also equally important

112
00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:52.200
is that as you get to work,

113
00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:55.280
you start to get to this stage of informed pessimism.

114
00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:57.200
So you start to learn more and you realize

115
00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.040
it may be harder than what you expect

116
00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:01.680
and a bit of doubt creeps into that psyche.

117
00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:04.280
And you may sometimes question if this is for you or not.

118
00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:07.160
And for some people, maybe you will get into this valley

119
00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:08.400
of despair is what they call it,

120
00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.240
which is the lowest point where you feel stuck

121
00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:12.360
or maybe overwhelmed or maybe ready to quit.

122
00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:14.960
But if you push true from it and you get to stage four,

123
00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:16.320
which is inform optimism,

124
00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:18.120
then things suddenly start to click

125
00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:19.440
because you build real skills,

126
00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:21.920
you start to see progress and you know that you can do this.

127
00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:23.720
And this is very important in our field

128
00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:25.480
because if you may have noticed in AI,

129
00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:27.400
a lot of new models, a lot of new tools

130
00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.320
come about like every month or so.

131
00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:30.800
And so once you get to that stage

132
00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:32.320
where you actually start to learn more

133
00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:34.760
and you realize that there's even more to learn,

134
00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:37.560
that is sometimes what gets you from here to here.

135
00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:38.960
But I think the key insight is

136
00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.200
if you are in uninformed optimism now,

137
00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.880
simply knowing and expecting that you may transition

138
00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:45.960
to this curve and hit this valley.

139
00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.760
Just know that that is completely normal

140
00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:49.760
and it's experienced by a lot of people.

141
00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.520
It's been true since the 1970s

142
00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:52.440
and it's still true today.

143
00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:54.120
And the only way out is true.

144
00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:56.040
So my advice is to keep pushing on

145
00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:57.960
because the core topic that we are teaching

146
00:04:57.960 --> 00:04:59.800
which is using artificial intelligence

147
00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:01.840
to build out solutions which will get into more

148
00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:04.800
in the succeeding models cannot really be undersold.

149
00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:06.520
It is a transformative technology

150
00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:07.720
that will change the world.

151
00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:11.400
The second principle is reps or repetitions over perfection.

152
00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:12.840
And this is actually the fastest way

153
00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.600
through the valley that we just talked about.

154
00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:16.680
It's basically volume, the volume of actions,

155
00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:18.160
the volume of shots that you take

156
00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:20.440
and with a lot of the tools that we'll introduce later on,

157
00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:22.400
especially when we talk about using content

158
00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:25.280
to build yourself some leverage and attract clients,

159
00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:26.880
there's actually no limit to how much

160
00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:28.160
that you can try in there.

161
00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:29.680
It's free to post on socials.

162
00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:32.400
And so this concept of using volume to your advantage

163
00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:34.240
is definitely something that you shouldn't miss.

164
00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:35.360
So you should learn by doing,

165
00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:36.800
not by planning the perfect thing.

166
00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:39.360
And this is something that is personally true for me as well

167
00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:40.840
because for the RoboNogus brand,

168
00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.160
we were able to grow it from literally zero followers

169
00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:45.880
at the beginning to something above 400K plus followers

170
00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:48.720
across socials and in our newsletter at this point.

171
00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:50.080
And the key thing that I wanted to highlight

172
00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:51.640
is that I also started from zero.

173
00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:54.560
So I've been personally in the AI space since I did my masters

174
00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:56.360
in data science from like six years ago,

175
00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:57.360
so over half a decade.

